/-! ## The molecular point group of benzene

Benzene (C₆H₆) is a planar regular hexagon, whose point group is `D₆ₕ`.
As an abstract group `D₆ₕ ≅ D₆ × Cᵢ`, i.e. the dihedral group of order `12`
(the symmetries of the hexagon) times the two-element group generated by the
inversion centre `i`. -/

/-- The point group `D₆ₕ`, realized as `D₆ × Cᵢ` (a group of order `24`). -/
abbrev D6h : Type := DihedralGroup 6 × Multiplicative (ZMod 2)

/-- The order of `D₆ₕ` is `24`. -/

theorem sum_sq_d6hDim : ∑ i : Fin 12, d6hDim i ^ 2 = 24 := by decide

/-- **Benzene / `D₆ₕ` irreducible representations.**

The character table of the benzene point group `D₆ₕ` (`≅ D₆ × Cᵢ`, of order `24`)
has the correct number of irreducible representations: there are exactly `12`
rows, matching the `12` conjugacy classes of `D₆ₕ`.  Moreover the tabulated data
really is a complete character table:

* the tabulated class sizes are the true conjugacy class sizes of `D₆ₕ`, and sum
  to the group order `24`;
* the rows are orthonormal with respect to the class-weighted inner product
  (row orthogonality), hence pairwise distinct;
* the columns satisfy the dual (column) orthogonality relations;
* the dimensions `1,1,1,1,2,2,1,1,1,1,2,2` satisfy `∑ dᵢ² = |D₆ₕ| = 24`. -/
